  "stage": "A09 Monte Carlo C ABI and Python callback snapshots",
  "base_commit": "8fc3710fc620403d1811fdb813afa97f5d7bd11e",
  "implementation": [
    "Seven additive C ABI exports with existing ABI layouts unchanged",
    "Synchronous multi-metric evaluator and cancellation; native sampler/statistics unchanged",
    "Owned immutable result handle; metadata-only queries and atomic capacity/overlap validation",
    "Input and options arrays frozen before callbacks; nested RFModel calls supported",
    "Python immutable snapshots with explicit None values and deterministic handle release",
    "Strict uint64 seeds, bounded iterables, UTF-8 diagnostics and fatal exception propagation",
    "Installed C consumer and installed Python wheel exercise Monte Carlo",
    "Python RF resistor tolerance JSON trace independently checks every circuit evaluation"
  ],
  "independent_checks": [
    "C buffer tail preservation, capacity overflow, alias rejection and unchanged failed outputs",
    "Callbacks cannot mutate copied distribution, quantile or criteria state",
    "Incorrect metric counts, incomplete writes, nonfinite output and bounded error text",
    "Sampling versus evaluation counters; stop/reject/cancel and pass fraction denominators",
    "Golden MT sequence, six distributions, recording-independent replay and extreme statistics",
    "Python fatal/cancel/exception-formatting errors and cleanup after result-copy failures",
    "Same-seed C++ and installed Python RF parameter traces identical; values checked within 1e-12",
    "Independent Python statistics and sorted quantiles recomputed from analytic circuit values"
  ],
